        "author": "<LINKEDIN_ORG_URN>",
        "commentary": "In some niche roles, Turkey pays higher salaries than every European country except 2-3.\n\nWage increases made during the cheap-financing era were a good thing — no argument there. But once financing costs spike, sustaining those raises gets a lot harder. As policy rates flow through to borrowing costs, businesses can no longer keep pace with wage growth while balancing cash flow.\n\nThere's also a composition problem: same seniority, same expertise, same role, same company profile — and pay in Turkey still outpaces most of Europe.\n\nDoes this signal a loss of skilled talent, or is it just a politically charged narrative? According to the data, this is measurable: how many people are leaving, is it 1% or 10%, and are they coming back?\n\nHow is your organization managing wage policy under today's financing cost pressure?\n\nhttps://www.datassist.com.tr/?utm_source=linkedin&utm_medium=social_organic&utm_campaign=datassist_clips&utm_content=c05&utm_term=data_number&yvc_v=A&yvc_lang=en\n\n#ücretlendirme #İK #bordro #ücretpolitikası #insankaynakları",
